description: Synthetic-data and assumption rules for process sketches
alwaysApply: true
---

# Data boundaries

- Treat ACME and every person in the input as fictional.
- Use only the input description and public or synthesized data. Never use real customer, candidate or employee data.
- Label every synthesized value `SYNTHETIC`.
- Label every value you assume yourself (not in the input) `ASSUMED`.
- Never invent a number the customer gave a different value for. If the input doesn't say, write "Not stated".
- Keep the speaker's words for pains. Don't make them sound worse or better.
- Never put secrets, tokens or env var values into a sketch.
